---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import ReviewNotice from '../components/ReviewNotice.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy | TGM Group"
  description="How TGM Group collects, uses and protects personal information, in line with the Protection of Personal Information Act."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }])]}
>
  <PageHero
    accent="navy"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lead="How we handle personal information, and what you can require of us under the Protection of Personal Information Act."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <ReviewNotice>
          It states what the website actually does, but the retention periods,
          the information officer's details and the operator arrangements must
          be confirmed by Trevor and reviewed by an attorney before launch.
        </ReviewNotice>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {site.name} is the responsible party for the personal information
          described here. You can reach us at
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or
          <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Information officer:</strong>
          <span class="placeholder">[Name and contact details]</span>. Under
          POPIA every responsible party must register an information officer
          with the Information Regulator. Confirm this is done and record the
          details here.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect two kinds of information, and no more than that.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>What you send us.</strong> If you complete the enquiry form
            or email us, we receive your name, work email address, organisation,
            the problem category you selected and anything you wrote in the
            message field.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>What the website records.</strong> This site is static and
            carries no advertising trackers, no analytics cookies and no
            third-party scripts. Our host keeps standard server logs, which
            include IP addresses, for security and availability purposes.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use cookies for tracking. We do not build profiles. We do
          not sell or rent personal information to anyone, under any
          circumstances.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we hold it, and for how long</h2>
        <p>
          We use what you send to respond to your enquiry, to prepare for a
          discovery call and, if we go on to work together, to run the
          engagement. That is the whole purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Retention:</strong> enquiries that do not lead to work are
          kept for 24 months and then deleted. Records relating to an actual
          engagement are kept for the period South African law requires for business records (<span class="placeholder">[confirm period with accountant]</span>) and then deleted.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
        <p>
          Two third parties handle your information on our instruction. Both act
          as operators under POPIA and are bound to protect it.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Formspree</strong> (Formspree, Inc.) processes our enquiry
            form. When you submit it, what you typed is transmitted to and
            stored on Formspree's servers in the <strong>United States</strong>,
            and forwarded to our email address.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Our email provider.</strong> Mail sent to our published
            address is handled by the mail platform attached to our domain
            registration.
            <span class="placeholder">[Name the email host and its country]</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Transfer outside South Africa</h3>
        <p>
          Because Formspree stores submissions in the United States, using the
          enquiry form transfers your personal information outside South Africa.
          Section 72 of POPIA permits this where the data subject consents to
          the transfer, and the consent checkbox on the form is that consent. It
          is required rather than optional for exactly that reason: without it
          there is no lawful basis to send your details abroad, so the form will
          not accept a submission without it.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would prefer your information stayed in South Africa, do not
          use the form. Email or telephone us instead, using the details in this
          policy, and say so.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under POPIA you may, at any time and at no cost:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Ask what personal information we hold about you</li>
          <li>Ask us to correct anything that is wrong</li>
          <li>Ask us to delete it, where we are not required to keep it</li>
          <li>Object to our processing it</li>
          <li>
            Complain to the Information Regulator if you are not satisfied with
            how we responded
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will
          respond within 30 days. Our
          <a href="/paia/">PAIA manual</a> sets out the formal access procedure.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable technical and organisational steps to protect
          personal information. This website is served over HTTPS only. If a
          breach affecting your information occurs, we will notify you and the
          Information Regulator as POPIA requires.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes materially we will say so on this page and
          update the date below.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Last updated:</strong>
          <span class="placeholder">[Date of legal sign-off]</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
